# This repo lives directly inside ~/.claude, which also holds credentials,
# prompt history, and full session transcripts. So: ignore EVERYTHING by
# default, then re-allow only the files that belong to the status line.
#
# Never convert this to a blocklist. The allowlist is what guarantees a
# stray `git add -A` can't publish .credentials.json, history.jsonl,
# projects/, sessions/, or shell-snapshots/.
*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!install.mjs
!statusline.mjs
!session-activity.mjs
